Substitute \( x = 2 \):

\[ g(2) = 2^2 + 3 \]
\[ g(2) = 4 + 3 \]
\[ g(2) = 7 \]

Next, we need to find \( f(g(2)) \), which is \( f(7) \):

\[ f(x) = 2x - 4 \]

Substitute \( x = 7 \):

\[ f(7) = 2(7) - 4 \]
\[ f(7) = 14 - 4 \]
\[ f(7) = 10 \]

Therefore, \( f(g(2)) = 10 \).

