Problem:
A tree is now 12 feet tall and grows 18 inches a year. In how many years will the tree be 36 feet tall?

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to convert the height of the tree from feet to inches because the growth rate is given in inches.

- Current height of the tree: \(12 \text{ feet} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} = 144 \text{ inches}\)
- Desired height of the tree: \(36 \text{ feet} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} = 432 \text{ inches}\)

Next, we calculate the total growth needed to reach the desired height:
\[ 432 \text{ inches} - 144 \text{ inches} = 288 \text{ inches} \]

The tree grows 18 inches per year. To find out how many years it will take for the tree to grow 288 inches, we divide the total growth needed by the annual growth rate:
\[ \frac{288 \text{ inches}}{18 \text{ inches/year}} = 16 \text{ years} \]

Therefore, the tree will take \(\boxed6166 for the tree to be 36 feet tall.
