answer:  If Denali started walking $4x$ more dogs and Nate stayed at $12$ dogs, Denali would walk $16 + 4x$ dogs and Nate would walk $12$ dogs. If $x$ of Nate's dogs were reassigned to Denali, Denali would walk $16 + x$ dogs and Nate would walk $12 - x$ dogs. The ratio of Denali's pay to Nate's pay would be the same in both cases, so we have:

