\[ 21^2 = 441 \text{ square centimeters} \]

The initial side length of the square is $1$ centimeter, so the area of the initial square is:

\[ 1^2 = 1 \text{ square centimeters} \]

The difference between the area of the last square and the area of the initial square is:

\[ 441 - 1 = 440 \text{ square centimeters} \]

Therefore, the difference between the area of the last square and the area of the initial square after $10$ minutes is:

\[ \44 \4440 \]

Final Answer: The final answer is $440 I hope it is correct.
