answer:  To find the smallest integer \( n \) for which the sum of the integers from \(-25\) to \( n \) (including \(-25\) and \( n \)) is at least \(26\), we start by calculating the sum of the integers from \(-25\) to \( n \).

The sum of the integers from \(-25\) to \( n \) can be expressed as:
\[
n - (-25) + 1 = n + 26
\]

