Since the degree of the left-hand side of the equation is the sum of the degrees of the two polynomials being multiplied, and the degree of \( x^2 - 1 \) is 2, the degree of \( f(x)) \) be be 6.

Thus, the degree of \( f(x) \) is \(\boxed{6}\).
