D=(0,120);
E=(-6.2,-8);
F=(60,90);
G=(70,105);

dot(F);

draw(A--B,Arrows);
draw(C--D,Arrows);
draw(E--G,Arrows);

label("(20,30)",G,SE);
label("$y=1.5x$",G,N);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  To determine how many meters Caroline will walk in exactly one hour, we need to use the given linear relationship between the time in seconds, \( x \), and the distance in meters, \( y \). The relationship is described by the equation \( y = 1.5x \).

