answer:  To find the graph of \( y = f^{-1}(x) \), we need to reflect the graph of \( y = f(x) \) over the line \( y = x \). This means that every point \((a, b)\) on the graph of \( y = f(x) \) will map to the point \((b, a)\) on the graph of \( y = f^{-1}(x) \).

