Solution:
answer:  We can write the left-hand side as
\[\frac{4x^3 - 20x^2 + 37x - 25}{(x-2)^3(x-1)} = \frac{A(x-2)^3 + B(x-2)^2 + C(x-2) + D(x-1)}{(x-2)^3(x-1)}.\]
Thus, we have
\[4x^3 - 20x^2 + 37x - 25 = A(x-2)^3 + B(x-2)^2 + C(x-2) + D(x-1).\]
Expanding the right-hand side, we get
\[4x^3 - 20x^2 + 37x - 25 = A(x-2)^3 + B(x-2)^2 + C(x-2) + D(x-1).\]
By comparing coefficients, we find that $A = 4,$ $B = -4,$ $C = 1,$ and $D = = =.$.$

