3. Subtract $x^3-3x^2$ from $x^3-3x^2-9x+30$ to get $6x^2-9x+30$.
4. Divide $6x^2$ by $x$ to get $6x$.
5. Multiply $6x$ by $x-3$ to get $6x^2-18x$.
6. Subtract $6x^2-18x$ from $6x^2-9x+30$ to get $9x+30$.
