answer:  We need to find the minimum value of the expression \(|z - 3|^2 + |z - 5 + 2i|^2 + |z - 1 + i|^2\). This expression represents the sum of the squares of the distances from a complex number \(z\) to the points \(3\), \(5 + 2i\), and \(1 - i\) in the complex plane.

The minimum value of the sum of the squares of the distances from a point to three given points in the complex plane is achieved when the point lies on the Fermat point of the triangle formed by these points. However, in this case, the points \(3\), \(5 + 2i\), and \(1 - i\) are collinear, so the Fermat point is the midpoint of the segment connecting these points.

The midpoint of the segment connecting \(3\) and \(5 + 2i\) is:
\[
