\[
ab + bc + ca \geq 3\sqrt[3]{216} = 3 \cdot 6 = 18
\]

Equality holds when \(a = b = c\). Therefore, the minimum value of \(ab + bc + ca\) is 18.

Thus, the smallest possible surface area of the box is:
\[
2(ab + bc + ca) = 2 \cdot 18 = 36
\]

