Problem:
The range of the function $f(x)$ is $[-3,5].$  Let $h(x) = 2f(x) - 7.$  Find the range of the function $h(x).$

Solution:
answer:  To find the range of the function \( h(x) = 2f(x) - 7 \), we start by considering the range of \( f(x) \), which is given as \([-3, 5]\).

First, we determine the range of \( 2f(x) \). Since \( f(x) \) can take any value from \(-3\) to \(5\), \( 2f(x) \) can take any value from \( 2(-3) \) to \( 2(5) \).

\[
2(-3) = -6 \quad \text{and} \quad 2(5) = 10
\]

Thus, the range of \( 2f(x) \) is \([-6, 10]\).

Next, we subtract 7 from each value in the interval \([-6, 10]\) to find the range of \( h(x) \).

\[
-6 - 7 = -1 \quad \text{and} \quad  0 - 7 = 3
\]

Therefore, the range of \( h(x) \) is \(\boxed{[-1, 3}\).
