Now, we need to find the remainder when $\phi(2^n)$ is divided by $13$.

We know that $2^n \equiv 3 \pmod{13}$, so we can use the property of Euler's totient function that $\phi(p) \equiv p-1 \pmod{p}$ for any prime $p$.

In this case, $p = 13$, so $\phi(13) \equiv 13-1 \pmod{13} \equiv 12 \pmod{13}$.

Therefore, the remainder when $\phi(2^n by is divided by $13$ is divided by $11$ isboxed{11}$.

