Problem:
What is the remainder when $129^{34}+96^{38}$ is divided by $11$?

Solution:
answer:  First, we find the remainder when $129^{34}$ is divided by $11$. Notice that $129 \equiv 1 \pmod{11}$, so $129^{34} \equiv 1^{34} \equiv 1 \pmod{11}$.

